  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 459586355200
    m_Localized: HOW TO FIND THE RIGHT SHELF FOR A TAPE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 459615715328
    m_Localized: "Each VHS tape belongs to a specific subgenre.\n\n\u2022 Check the
      cover, title, and sticker to identify the tape\u2019s subgenre.\n\u2022 Find
      the shelf with the matching label. Subgenre labels also have stickers \u2014
      compare them with the one on the tape.\n\u2022 Place the tape on the correct
      shelf.\n\nYou can use any empty slot on the matching shelf. A glow and a sound
      will confirm correct placement.\n\nSunset Creek tapes are the exception: their
      order matters.\n"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 459615715329
    m_Localized: "HOW TO IDENTIFY A TAPE\u2019S GENRE USING THE VCR"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 459615715330
    m_Localized: "If you\u2019re unsure where a tape belongs, the VCR can help narrow
      down your search.\n\n\u2022 Insert the tape into the VCR.\n\u2022 Watch the
      short clip and read the genre name that appears.\n\u2022 Find that genre\u2019s
      section, then use the tape\u2019s cover, title, and sticker to identify the
      right subgenre.\n\nThe VCR reveals only the genre. You\u2019ll still need to
      work out the subgenre and find the correct shelf yourself.\n"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 459615715331
    m_Localized: HOW TO COLLECT TAPES RETURNED BY CUSTOMERS
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 459615715332
    m_Localized: "Customers call and return tapes as you make progress with sorting.\n\n\u2022
      When the phone rings, answer it and talk to the customer.\n\u2022 Keep sorting
      tapes.\n\u2022 When a returned tape arrives, collect it from the box by the
      door and find its correct shelf.\n\nNew events depend on how many tapes you\u2019ve
      sorted. Keep sorting to receive more calls, returned tapes, and gifts. Gifts
      appear beside the box, rather than inside it.\n"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 459615715335
    m_Localized: HOW TO DECORATE THE STORE WITH GIFTS FROM CUSTOMERS
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 459615715336
    m_Localized: "Sometimes, customers leave gifts to make the store feel cozier.\n\n\u2022
      Pick up a gift by the door.\n\u2022 Its designated spot will light up when
      you pick it up.\n\u2022 Take the gift to the highlighted spot and place it.\n\nEach
      gift has a designated spot. Once placed, it cannot be moved or removed.\n"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 459615715337
    m_Localized: HOW TO CHANGE THE MUSIC IN THE STORE
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 459615715338
    m_Localized: "Audio cassettes let you choose the music while you sort.\n\n\u2022
      Select an audio cassette on the shelf above the cassette player.\n\u2022 Press
      Play on the player to start the selected music.\n\u2022 To change the music,
      select another cassette and press Play again.\n\nLook around the store for
      more audio cassettes. The ones you find will appear on the shelf above the
      cassette player.\n\n"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9846588025028608
    m_Localized: HOW TO PUT SUNSET CREEK EPISODES IN ORDER
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9846588054388736
    m_Localized: "Sunset Creek is a TV series whose tapes must be arranged in story
      order.\n\n\u2022 Watch the show\u2019s tapes on the VCR.\n\u2022 Compare the
      events in each episode to work out what happened earlier and what happened
      later.\n\u2022 Place each tape in its corresponding slot on the show\u2019s
      shelving unit.\n\nThese are the only tapes that require a specific slot. If
      you\u2019re unsure about the sequence, watch the episodes again on the VCR.\n"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
